An agent file's maxTurns is now honoured, and yoyo agents no longer claims these agents go unused. It's committed as c1205469. cargo fmt --check, clippy with -D warnings and the full cargo test all pass.

• The turn cap: when the agent tool builds a child, it now applies the file's maxTurns after the shared default of 25, so the file's value wins. A file without maxTurns keeps 25. That default is yoyo's own choice, not a Claude Code value, and the commit body says so. When a child hits its cap, yoagent adds its own [Agent stopped: …] notice, so I didn't build a counter or a "partial" marker.
• Invalid values: maxTurns: 0 used to load, because the check only rejected negative numbers. It is now skipped with "maxTurns 0 is not a positive whole number". Negatives, decimals and strings were already skipped; I added test rows for each. Large values are used as written. One leftover: a number above about 4.29 billion is also skipped, with the same "not a positive whole number" message, which is a bit misleading for such a value.
• The listing: the header now reads "Named sub-agents (the model can delegate to these with the agent tool; project-scope ones only with --trust-project; none whose tools resolve to nothing)". A row's model: X now carries "(not honoured yet: runs on sub_agent_model, else the main model)", which matches what the child actually runs on.
• Tests: yoagent's SubAgentTool has no way to read its turn cap back, so the test runs a real one on yoagent's mock provider, scripted for 6 tool calls. With maxTurns: 3 exactly 3 run and the stop notice appears. With no maxTurns all 6 run and the child finishes on its own text. I disabled the call as a positive control (marked NEUTERED, in one mutate→run→restore command); the test failed by name, then passed again once restored.
• Docs: docs/src/usage/commands.md, the src/agent_dispatch.rs comments and the ARCHITECTURE.md entries for both files are updated. The old claims are marked superseded, not erased.

I posted on #1250 what landed and what's next: the model half of milestone 3, meaning which model wins (the agent file, sub_agent_model or the main model) and a rule for haiku/sonnet/opus names on non-Anthropic providers.

.yoyo/risk_weights.json was already modified before I started, so I left it out of the commit rather than use git add -A. It's still uncommitted.
